---
description: Team rules from .claude/rules, which Cursor does not load on its own
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never push directly to `main`; always use a feature branch and PR.
- Never merge a PR without explicit approval in this conversation.
- Never discard uncommitted changes (`git restore`, `checkout --`, `clean -f`, `reset --hard`, `git stash drop`) without confirming. Leave unrelated changes alone or re-stash them.
- No `Co-Authored-By` trailers in commits.
- Don't add banner comments at the top of source files; exemptions in `.claude/rules/no-top-of-file-comments.md`.
- When opening PRs or issues, read `.claude/rules/pull-requests.md` and `.claude/rules/github-issues.md`.

Sources: `no-merge-prs.md`, `never-discard-changes.md`, `no-co-authored-by.md`, `no-top-of-file-comments.md`. Path-scoped rules attach through the generated `claude-rule-*.mdc` files.
